From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z5vix <z5vix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UWP Store: Minecraft start-up fixes, GDK installs and title sign-in from the store

- kernelbase/ntdll: ResolveDelayLoadsFromDll (LdrResolveDelayLoadsFromDll); Minecraft calls it at start.
- windows.devices.enumeration: CreateFromIdAsync, with the local machine container always present.
- windows.ui.core.textinput: CoreInputView answers "no touch keyboard" instead of E_NOTIMPL.
- combase: ordinal 133 RoIsASTAWorkScheduledAtPriorityOrHigher takes one argument and returns BOOL, as Windows'.
- xgameruntime: XSystemGetAnalyticsInfo (class b884675d...), which returns its struct by value; the generic stub
  gave GDK games a NULL and Minecraft crashed at start.
- winexboxauth:
  * XboxAuthImportRefreshToken: the store signs the prefix in with its own Microsoft account (same client id) and
    installs GDK titles without the Xbox app.
  * XboxAuthImportClientRefreshToken / XboxAuthHasClient: a game's own MSAAppId sign-in, run by the store as a
    device-code sign-in once per account; kept with the account it belongs to.
  * sisu_client_for: MSAAppIds that only Windows' account broker redeems (SISU 401) get their title tokens through
    the same game's SISU client (Minecraft for Windows 0000000040159362 -> 0000000048183522), and title endpoints
    come from that client's title, which maps *.playfabapi.com to Minecraft's PlayFab relying party.
  * XboxAuthGetTokenAndSignature: success with an empty token for a URL with no relying party (it ran strlen on
    NULL and crashed the caller).
  * take_msa_tokens: a refresh that names no user no longer blanks the stored user_id (the game's process never
    read it, and XboxAuthHasClient then took the account's own client sign-in for another account's).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
